<p>In today's business world, understanding customers is very important for successful marketing. Customer segmentation helps companies divide customers into groups based on similar characteristics like age, income, spending habits, and responses to marketing. This allows businesses to create better offers and improve customer satisfaction. In this assignment, we will use three popular clustering methods — K-Means, DBSCAN, and Agglomerative Clustering — to group customers using real-world marketing data. The process will include exploring, cleaning, and normalizing the data, applying clustering techniques, and using PCA to visualize the results. In the end, we will identify meaningful customer groups that can help businesses make smarter and more targeted decisions.</p>
