<h4 id="A.-Elbow-Method-using-K-Means-to-Find-Optimal-Number-of-Clusters"><strong>A. Elbow Method using K-Means to Find Optimal Number of Clusters</strong><a class="anchor-link" href="#A.-Elbow-Method-using-K-Means-to-Find-Optimal-Number-of-Clusters">¶</a></h4><p>Below code tests multiple k values (1 to 10) by fitting K-Means each time, calculates the Within-Cluster Sum of Squares (WCSS) for each k, and plots a curve to visually detect the "elbow point", which helps select the optimal number of clusters where adding more clusters doesn't significantly reduce the WCSS.</p>
</div>
