<h1 id="Conclusion">Conclusion<a class="anchor-link" href="#Conclusion">¶</a></h1><p>Through the application of K-Means, DBSCAN, and Agglomerative Clustering, we successfully segmented customers based on demographics, purchasing behavior, and marketing interactions. K-Means provided clear and balanced clusters, allowing us to identify high-income, high-spending customers, moderate spenders, and lower-income segments. DBSCAN was helpful in detecting outliers and smaller niche groups, which may hold valuable insights for targeting special customer segments. Agglomerative Clustering offered a hierarchical structure, giving us well-separated and interpretable clusters, distinguishing premium customers from budget-conscious families and moderate spenders. Overall, all three methods revealed meaningful customer patterns, highlighting how segmentation can help businesses tailor marketing strategies, design personalized offers, improve customer loyalty, and ultimately drive profitability.</p>
